TWO SEPARATE LAYERS — DO NOT CONFLATE THEM
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository contains the SOFTWARE of a fitness training application:
source code, database schema, interface copy, design and icons. All of it
is the property of Kevin Rincón and is protected by copyright law.

The TRAINING CONTENT the application displays when running — the
exercises, the technique cues, the routines, the programs and the recipes
— is NOT in this repository and is NOT owned by the software's copyright
holder. That content is the work of the trainer who wrote it, belongs to
him, and its use is governed by his decisions.

The sample data that IS in this repository (supabase/04-ejemplo.sql) is
invented for testing purposes. It is not any trainer's real content.

PERMITTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  • Using the application from its public address, installing it on your
    own phone.

  • Reading and studying the source code. It is public on purpose: so it
    can be learned from, and so the handling of personal data can be
    audited — which in an application holding health data is not a minor
    detail.

  • Quoting short excerpts with attribution, for example in an article, a
    class or a review.

NOT PERMITTED without the copyright holder's written authorization
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  • Copying, reproducing or redistributing the code, in whole or in part,
    beyond short quotation with attribution.

  • Modifying the code or creating derivative works from it.

  • Publishing the application, or a modified version of it, at another
    address, app store or repository.

  • Using the code for commercial purposes.

A public repository does NOT mean the code is public domain or free to
use. It is public by its author's choice, so that it can be read and
audited. There is no open-source license here: absent a license granting
otherwise, copyright is reserved by default.

To request permission: kevin.rincon1023@gmail.com
